Flight.proto, FlightSql.proto

Apache Arrow's Flight and Flight SQL protocols, copied unmodified from
apache/arrow at c07de67a7c (2026-09-18; the files last changed in
2cd5ad233fab, 2026-06-08), oss_databases/arrow/format/.  Apache License 2.0,
as their headers say; Apache Arrow's NOTICE:

  Apache Arrow
  Copyright 2016-2026 The Apache Software Foundation

  This product includes software developed at
  The Apache Software Foundation (http://www.apache.org/).

  sha256  ccd439108e960d83a285f759a3c2b7cd6432320b8491734d13f589edccf1d5b0  Flight.proto
          8e05bdf3a8e3bde84f2647bae31cf674b4790aa7068f1ab198cb25ee1656a5e5  FlightSql.proto

The build does not compile these files as they are.  protobuf-c 1.5.1, the
generator Debian 13 ships, refuses proto3's "optional" fields ("hasn't been
updated to support optional fields in proto3"), so transform.sh writes copies
into gen/ in which each

    optional T name = N;

is the one-field oneof protoc itself makes of it, which has the same wire
format and keeps the field's presence:

    oneof _name { T name = N; }

and FlightSql.proto's declaration of the "experimental" message option, which
nothing uses, is dropped with its import of google/protobuf/descriptor.proto.
Flight.proto's import of google/protobuf/timestamp.proto is generated from
protobuf's own copy, /usr/include/google/protobuf/timestamp.proto.
